<quest quest_id="312" category="lore_quest" tag="The Doombringer" published="False" valid="True">
	<title>The Doombringer</title>
	<description>You hadn&apos;t taken more than three steps into the dark and frosted chamber that housed the portal when Behrem&apos;s voice suddenly cracked like a whithin your mind!</description>
	<nodes>
		<node type="start_node" id="0" tag="">
			<conditions>
				<condition type="quest_completion" id="1" value="1" tag="A Quest Completion Condition" quest_id="311" />
			</conditions>
		</node>
		<node type="event_branch" id="1" tag="" />
		<node type="event_join" id="2" tag="Activate the Hand">
			<journal_entry>You&apos;d barely needed to touch the strange, hand-shaped altar and something happened.  Possibly the blood you&apos;d recently spilled was all that it needed but suddenly, an eerie buzz that you&apos;d not noticed on the edge of your hearing began to intensify.</journal_entry>
			<tasks>
				<task type="interact_with_object" id="3" value="1" tag="Activate the Hand Shaped Altar" resource_name="r_qt  darkbrood hand">
					<task_instruction>Activate the Hand Shaped Altar</task_instruction>
				</task>
			</tasks>
		</node>
		<node type="event_simple" id="3" tag="">
			<journal_entry>It was by no means an easy battle.  The Doombringer was not only an able foe but was driven by a malicious rage that filtered through every one of his Darkbrood minions.</journal_entry>
		</node>
		<node type="event_simple" id="4" tag="Fight the Doombringer">
			<instruction>Sustain damage from the Doombringer until the Hivemind has reacted.</instruction>
			<journal_entry>That seemed to do it! The chaos you&apos;d sown with the Darkbrood blood had acted as an amplifier for their hivemind and by surviving the Doombringer, the conduit for their collective, you had funneled all that chaos and panic right onto him.  Like a hive rejecting their queen, the Darkbrood would very soon descend upon him and finish what you began.</journal_entry>
			<tasks>
				<task type="take_damage_from" id="7" value="1" tag="Get hurt by Doombringer" magnitude="600" resource_name="r_Darkbrood Doombringer" />
			</tasks>
		</node>
		<node type="event_branch" id="5" tag="20 Vials of Blood">
			<journal_entry>With that grizzly task done, you now had enough blood to sow some chaos around the area.  Behrem had said that the Darkbrood&apos;s blood carried their collective voice and cursed insanity, the legacy of Sahul the fool.</journal_entry>
			<tasks>
				<task type="gather_items" id="9" value="1" tag="have vials" resource_name="r_Darkbrood Blood" quantity="20" inventory_type="Backpack">
					<task_instruction>Gather the 20 </task_instruction>
				</task>
			</tasks>
		</node>
		<node type="event_simple" id="6" tag="Kill the Doombringer">
			<journal_entry>Which is, as it turned out, exactly what you did! Preferring to stab right to the heart of the matter, as it were, you made your way directly to the Doombringer himself. The Ork&apos;s had decreed him guilty and sentenced him to death, a death that you were all too happy to provide!</journal_entry>
			<tasks>
				<task type="kill_object" id="8" value="1" tag="Kill the Doombringer" resource_name="r_Darkbrood Doombringer" quantity="1" />
			</tasks>
		</node>
		<node type="event_simple_conditional" id="7" tag="Smear Blood fanatic" optional_tasks="False">
			<conditions>
				<condition type="item_possession" id="0" value="3" tag="Have Blood" resource_name="r_Darkbrood Blood" quantity="2" inventory_type="Backpack" />
			</conditions>
			<tasks>
				<task type="activate_item" id="19" value="1" tag="An Activate Item Task" resource_name="r_Darkbrood Blood" consume="False">
					<task_instruction>Use the blood near a $[Resource.D.r_darkbrood_fanatic_NameSingular]</task_instruction>
				</task>
				<task type="go_near_object" id="16" value="1" tag="A Go Near Object Task" resource_name="r_Darkbrood Fanatic" distance="15" />
			</tasks>
		</node>
		<node type="event_simple" id="8" tag="">
			<journal_entry>There was, however, something more.  The Acolyte was correct it seemed, he was more than just Darkbrood; he was somehow enhanced, imbued with a power far beyond his own.</journal_entry>
		</node>
