		<node type="event_simple" id="27" tag="">
			<journal_entry>Once you had sufficiently regained your composure and staved off the looming heart attack, you took a moment to listen to his frenzied whispering.</journal_entry>
		</node>
		<node type="event_simple" id="28" tag="">
			<journal_entry>&quot;Hssst! Hold! You must listen to me friend! Heed my words before you doom us all! I speak to you now through the Orkish emmisaries fire ritual...tis a most fascinating example of primitive energy relocation that I must...ehem, I digress!</journal_entry>
		</node>
		<node type="event_simple" id="29" tag="">
			<journal_entry>The Orks do not understand the full extent of the Doombringer! While you were gone, I have been pouring over certain texts and dark writings.  The Doombringer is indeed the conduit to the Darkbrood&apos;s hive mind, but he has also been exponentially enhanced! The Darkbrood are incabable of such planning as we have witnessed, they are but pawns, hired hands if you will.  The Doombringer is their reward! One of their own given such power as to stand above the rest and, in essence, give them what they could never have as a collective.  A leader!</journal_entry>
		</node>
		<node type="event_simple" id="30" tag="">
			<journal_entry>Therein lies both the rub and your salvation! The Doombringer, I believe, is far beyond your capabilities.  If I am wrong, then by all means, slay him to death! If, however, I am correct, then I believe I have a better way...</journal_entry>
		</node>
		<node type="event_simple" id="31" tag="">
			<journal_entry>The Doombringer, as I said, acts as a conduit for the hive mind.  This, I believe, can be his undoing! The hive mentality of the Darkbrood gives us a weapon against them.  The secret lies in their blood...&quot;</journal_entry>
		</node>
		<node type="event_simple" id="32" tag="">
			<journal_entry>He went on at some length, going into various grizzlt details and describing how the Darkbrood&apos;s blood held their hive voice.  Smearing it around the area and burning it on their specially attuned forges should create a confusion and chaos.  Activating their hand-shaped altar would focus and resonate that chaos.</journal_entry>
		</node>
		<node type="event_simple" id="33" tag="">
			<journal_entry>It seemed your next step would be in the collection of Darkbrood blood! That, or you could, of course simply have ignored the Acolyte all togther and battled the Doombringer yourself.</journal_entry>
		</node>
		<node type="event_simple" id="34" tag="">
			<journal_entry>While there was no doubt that you had struck a definitive blow against a dark power behind much of what you had witnessed of late, there was still a very frustrating lack of motive and reasoning behind it all.</journal_entry>
		</node>
		<node type="event_simple" id="35" tag="">
			<journal_entry>There was another, bigger player behind the curtain and, given time, you would find them! Trust me on this...</journal_entry>
		</node>
